# Example OpenSSH Server Configuration for SRUI Subsystem (§19, §19.1, §20.1)
#
# Add this snippet to /etc/ssh/sshd_config or /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/srui.conf
#
# When a client connects via `ssh <host> -s srui`, sshd launches srui-ssh-bridge
# under the authenticated user's OS privileges with standard I/O wired to the
# SSH channel. The bridge transparently proxies framed protocol bytes to the
# user's private session daemon socket (srui-sessiond.sock).
#
# Format:
#   Subsystem <subsystem_name> <path_to_binary> [<arguments>...]

# The runtime directory holding the socket must be a real directory (not a symlink) owned by the
# authenticated user with mode 0700, and the bridge refuses effective UID 0 (§27). Shared
# directories such as /tmp itself are refused; the no-XDG fallback is a per-user subdirectory.

# Default configuration (connects to $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/srui-sessiond.sock, or
# $TMPDIR/srui-<uid>/srui-sessiond.sock when XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is unset):
Subsystem srui /usr/local/bin/srui-ssh-bridge

# Or specify a custom socket path explicitly:
# Subsystem srui /usr/local/bin/srui-ssh-bridge /run/user/1000/srui-sessiond.sock
# Subsystem srui /usr/local/bin/srui-ssh-bridge --socket /run/user/1000/srui-sessiond.sock
